  "narrative": "The independent validation for H5 supports the discovery finding: SMARCA4-loss cells have a lower composite dependency score than non-deleted cells, reported as a signed effect of +0.795 in the hypothesized negative-dependency direction, with interval +0.695 to +0.896. This is far above the 0.15 threshold and consistent with the discovery estimate +0.833 [0.767, 0.898], though slightly attenuated. I therefore accept H5 as a reproducible dataset association between SMARCA4 loss and stronger measured dependency. This is not a causal or generalizable biological claim; the state may be correlated with other genomic or technical features.\n\nThe current main supported associations are: TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency (H3, +0.423 [0.327, 0.520]); SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency (H5, discovery +0.833 [0.767, 0.898], validation +0.795 [0.695, 0.896]); and KEAP1 loss associated with weaker dependency (H7, +0.832 [0.766, 0.897]). The negative findings are lineage subtype, KRAS mutation, MTAP loss, PIK3CA mutation, MYC amplification, all three constructed markers as main effects, and the KRAS-by-marker-D interaction; each estimate was near zero and incompatible with a scientifically meaningful claimed-direction effect.\n\nThe most important unresolved issue is whether the large SMARCA4 and KEAP1 associations are independent or mutually confounded, and whether TP53 loss contributes independently once those states are excluded. I registered and plan to run the conditional comparisons H13-H17 plus additional screens H18-H23. I also added a stratum-specific SMARCA4-loss comparison within KEAP1-loss-positive lines to characterize the effect in the overlap region. The next analysis should clarify whether SMARCA4 loss remains strongly negative when KEAP1 loss is absent, whether KEAP1 loss remains strongly positive when SMARCA4 loss is absent, and whether the library technical factor induces substantial mean shifts.",
  "research_notes": "Supported findings: H3 TP53_loss -> higher dependency_composite/weaker dependency, +0.423 [0.327,0.520]; H5 SMARCA4_loss -> stronger dependency, discovery +0.833 [0.767,0.898], independent validation +0.795 [0.695,0.896]; H7 KEAP1_loss -> higher composite/weaker dependency, +0.832 [0.766,0.897]. Negative: H1 lineage, H2 KRAS, H4 MTAP, H6 PIK3CA, H8 MYC amplification, H9-H11 markers D/E/F, H12 KRAS x marker D. Validation did not weaken H5 below threshold. Next priorities: run H13-H23 and proposed overlap-stratum SMARCA4 effect in KEAP1_loss=1. If conditional effects remain large, treat SMARCA4/KEAP1/TP53 as separable dataset associations. If attenuated, focus on whichever predictor dominates and consider interaction or overlap diagnostics. Continue confounding audit with library, culture/batch, growth/screen-quality variables if later needed."
